Interpretation:
- From P1: IPv4 with src in 10.0.2.0/24 and dst in 10.0.2.0/24 goes to P2. ARP goes to P2. Everything else from P1 goes only to P3.
- From P2: IPv4 to 10.0.2.0/24 goes to P1, and ARP goes to P1. Everything else from P2 is dropped, which is the default when nothing matches.

Whether intra-segment traffic should also be mirrored to the tap is not specified, so I send it only to P2. The "everything else" rule from P1 goes to P3 at low priority.

The intent says the uplink reaches P1 only for IPv4 to the segment and ARP, so the P2 rules are restricted to those. No rule matches other traffic from P2, so it is dropped.

